EXT. DUST STREET - GHOST TOWN - HIGH NOON

Sun like a hammer. Wind. A rusted sign creaks: "SALOON."

SHERIFF JEDEDIAH CROW (50s, tin star, dust-gray duster) stands in the middle of the road. Thumb on his hammer.

Forty feet away: MERCY BELLWEATHER (30s, black hat, two revolvers, one eyebrow cocked).

Neither moves.

CROW
Mercy.

MERCY
Jed.

CROW
You came back.

MERCY
Didn't plan to.

A tumbleweed rolls between them.

CROW
There's no one left to arrest.

MERCY
Then you're alone.

CROW
(to himself)
Always was.

Mercy's fingers twitch. Crow's too.

CROW (CONT'D)
(to the empty windows)
Anyone watching, step back.

Wind. A shutter bangs.

MERCY
Draw, Jed.

CROW
After you.

Neither draws. The sun climbs another degree. A fly lands on Crow's hat. Mercy smiles.

MERCY
Still a gentleman.

CROW
Still a fool.

She draws.
